---
title: Open, download and share a file
description: Preview a file, see its details and versions, download it, and send a colleague a link to it.
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

## Two ways to open a file

| Select | Opens |
|---|---|
| The file's name | The file in a full-page viewer, in a new tab. |
| Anywhere else on the file's row | **Document details** on the right of the library. |

## The viewer

The viewer shows the file with page thumbnails on the left (for PDFs and images). What you see depends on the type of file:

| File | Preview |
|---|---|
| PDF, PNG, JPEG | Shown as it is. For a PDF, use **Fit page**, **Fit width**, **Rotate left**, **Rotate right**, **Zoom out** and **Zoom in**, and type a page number to go to it. |
| Excel and CSV | A tab for each sheet. Very large sheets show only their first rows: download the file to see the rest. |
| Word and PowerPoint | Converted to PDF for viewing. **Preparing preview…** is shown while it is converted. Files over 15 MB are not previewed. |
| Other files | **Preview isn't available for this file — download it to view.** |

The top bar shows when the file was last modified and who uploaded it, its sensitivity, and **Download**. The panel on the right has two tabs:

- **Document info** — the folder, sensitivity, size, type and dates of the file.
- **Version history** — every version of the file. Select a version to view it.

## Document details

**Document details** on the right of the library shows the file's information (**Metadata**), its **Tags** and its versions (**Versions**). Under **Actions** are **Download**, **Rename** and **Delete**.

To add a new version of the file, select **+ Upload new version**. The new file keeps the name of the existing one, and earlier versions stay in the list.

## Download

Select **Download** in the viewer, in **Document details**, or in the file's **⋯** menu. To download several files, select them with the check boxes and then **Download**.

Some kinds of documents can be viewed in Operon but not downloaded. Then **Download** is greyed out with the reason, and files of this kind are skipped when you download several at once.

## Send a colleague a link

Select **Copy link** in the file's **⋯** menu and paste the link in a message to a colleague. The link opens the file in Operon for people who can see it; for anyone else it shows **This document does not exist, or this account may not open it**. There are no public links: files cannot be shared with people outside your firm from the library.

## Files from other parts of Operon

- **Bookkeeping:** documents uploaded in the bookkeeping workbench are filed in the company's **ACCOUNTS & TAX** folder, by financial year and month.
- **E-Sign:** signed copies from a case are filed in the case's **Signed** folder. To send a document for signature, use **E-Sign** (see [E-Sign](/en/e-sign/overview/)).
- **Chat:** files you attach in a chat with an AI employee are kept with the conversation, not in the library.
